        {
          "id": 3429011415,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Can a user without a development environment (i.e. compile Wireshark) \"manually\" tweak the files to correct a translation?  If not, then I agree they can probably be removed from (all) installations.",
          "author": {
            "id": 8399509,
            "username": "mmann78",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Michael Mann",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fad119898ba16a3f8be2f765dcff399098444abd4f85a04d4c3ef415a2bbe3d9?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/mmann78"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-06-06T16:32:23.325Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-06-06T16:32:23.325Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 464538809,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 23964,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 3429525047,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "So if we include the files, then a user can manually tweak the files to correct a translation, although they have to be put in the correct location.\n\nOur current search order for the translators is to look inside the resource system and then for files. For the \"wireshark\" specific translation files, it looks in the datafile (global) directory, under a `languages` subdirectory, and then personal configuration directory, also under a `languages` subdirectory. It only loads one version; they replace each other, with the last taking preference.\n\nThere's also the \"qt\" Qt-provided translation files. With recent Qt it is, I believe, possible to have the Qt provided translations merged into ours (https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/qtlinguist-cmake-qt-add-translations.html or https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/qtlinguist-cmake-qt-add-lrelease.html) but we don't do that, partially because that makes less sense on UN\\*X systems where there's shared libraries and the Qt-provided translations might be updated separately after our build. For those, it prefers the personal configuration directory, then the datafile directory (**but for each of these it does *not* look inside the `languages` subdirectory**), then the default location, which on a UN*X system is something like `/usr/share/qt6/translations` but which on the Windows installer is likely `C:\\Program Files\\Wireshark\\translations`. Note that putting the `qm` files in that directory by default does not make them used - they have to be altered and then placed in a different directory, e.g. `C:\\Program Files\\Wireshark\\languages`.\n\nThe WSDG discusses it a bit [here](https://www.wireshark.org/docs/wsdg_html_chunked/ChUIQt.html#ChUII18N) (which might need to be updated), but I don't think the User's Guide discusses how to change the translations in that way.\n\nAs another note, with the translations, Qt translations follow a practice of using the most recently installed translations first, so we probably want to install the Qt provided translations *first* and ours *last* (the reverse of the current order), so that our translations supersede.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-06-06T18:51:31.005Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-06-06T18:53:45.354Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 464538809,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 23964,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 3429534822,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "On any system where we ship and install the separate files, it's somewhat wasteful to embed them in the application as well. It would be especially pointless if we made it so that the search path was that the default qm files were always used, although selectively not embedding them depending on platform could be a bit fragile and lead to mistakes like accidentally not embedding them in a platform that doesn't install them.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-06-06T18:54:50.255Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-06-06T18:54:50.255Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 464538809,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 23964,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 3429562705,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "To me it sounds like we should not install translation files. But maybe describe how to add your own files. On the other hand we'll prefere people to contribute translations rather than keeping them to themselves",
          "author": {
            "id": 6792385,
            "username": "AndersBroman",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "AndersBroman",
