        {
          "id": 3429691383,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> So if we include the files, then a user can manually tweak the files to correct a translation\n\nIf this is something that's likely to happen, we should at least document a procedure by which the user can, at least, report the need for a correction, and perhaps even submit the correction as a change. (Does this involve Transifex in some fashion?)",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
