          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 3429696975,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> On the other hand we'll prefere people to contribute translations rather than keeping them to themselves\n\nYes. (I'd also prefer that downstream redistributors notify us of changes need to make Wireshark run on their platform; I decided to try building for Haiku, and extracted some of their changes and committed them in !25144; as per my comment there:\n\n> A programmer tweaked\\\n> They did not send it upstream\\\n> That one is on them",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-06-06T20:08:37.437Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-06-06T20:08:37.437Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 464538809,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 23964,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 3429727930,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Given that the QM files are a binary format, I don't think it makes a lot of sense to ship them in the installer if we're going to embed them. It makes it *slightly* easier for someone to tweak the source ts files, compile them with Qt Linguist and replace them, but very very slightly. They still have the option of doing that and putting the replacements in the directory - or, as noted, better yet, getting the translation fixed for everyone via Transifex.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
